# Model profile: Qwen3.8-27B (primary target -- plan-radiance-vllm.md §6)
#
# Same model family already running in production via llama.cpp on this
# host (unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF). Dense but architecturally hybrid: 16
# blocks of 3x(Gated DeltaNet -> FFN) -> 1x(Gated Attention -> FFN), hidden
# dim 5120, 64 layers, native context 262144. This hybrid architecture is
# the single biggest compatibility risk in this whole migration -- it is
# the documented root cause of multiple real bugs already hit on this host
# with this exact model family (see plan §6.2). Phase 0 must confirm this
# loads and generates coherent output on the vllm-radiance image BEFORE any
# of the settings below are trusted.
#
# MODEL_ID resolved via research 2026-09-14 (plan §24 open question 1,
# now answered): Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B is actually a VISION-LANGUAGE model
# (architectures: Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration, has a vision_config
# block) -- the language backbone matches the hybrid DeltaNet/Attention
# description, but --language-model-only (below) is required to avoid
# loading/profiling the vision tower, exactly like the sibling
# Qwen3.6-27B profile in the abandoned vLLM repo.
#
# *** CRITICAL FINDING (2026-09-14, from direct image inspection) ***
# vllm-radiance's own DOCKERHUB.md states verbatim: "Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 /
# Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 are what everything here is tuned around" -- i.e. the
# WHOLE Radiance/R4D/DFlash2 stack is qualified against the OFFICIAL FP8
# checkpoint (Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8, 30.89GB), not an INT4 quant. Their
# stated qualified weight formats are "native FP8 or AMD Quark MXFP4"
# specifically -- NOT generic AWQ/GPTQ/compressed-tensors INT4. This is a
# real tension with VRAM math: FP8 at 30.89GB leaves ~1GB for KV
# cache+overhead on this 32GB card -- essentially incompatible with the
# 131072-context target, and this is exactly the single-GPU-vs-the-
# 2-GPU-qualified-topology mismatch the plan already flagged as risk #2
# (plan §4, §9.4: the primary qualified environment is 2xR9700, combined
# 64GB VRAM, where 30GB FP8 weights + FP8 KV comfortably fits).
#
# Phase 0 resolves this empirically, in this order:
#   1. Try Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 with R4D+DFlash2 enabled and a SMALL
#      context (e.g. 8192) purely to confirm the architecture loads and
#      R4D actually engages for this model's 16 full-attention blocks --
#      this is the maintainer's actual tuned/tested target, highest odds
#      of R4D/DFlash2 working AT ALL. Not the final config even if it
#      works -- context is far too small.
#   2. If (1) works architecturally but can't fit 131072 context in 32GB
#      (expected), fall back to the INT4 compressed-tensors candidate
#      below for the real deployment, accepting R4D may hard-refuse at
#      startup for non-FP8/non-MXFP4 weights (plan §8.1's confirmed
#      fallback: set RADIANCE_USE_R4D=0 / RADIANCE_USE_R4D_GDN=0 in .env
#      and redeploy with standard attention if so).
#   3. amd/Qwen3.8-27B-Quark-AWQ-MXFP4 (19.82GB, Quark/MXFP4 format) is a
#      possible middle ground -- native MXFP4 is explicitly supported by
#      this image (RADIANCE_MXFP4 env var) and might let R4D/DFlash2
#      engage AND fit VRAM. Worth trying despite this project's past
#      Quark-loader crash on a different (older) vLLM build + different
#      checkpoint -- vllm-radiance's vLLM 0.28.0 is materially newer.
#
# INT4 fallback candidate (verified via its own raw config.json, never
# inferred from the repo name): RedHatAI/Qwen3.8-27B-INT4 --
# quant_method "compressed-tensors", format "pack-quantized", group_size
# 128, symmetric int4, 19.47GB. Red Hat AI / Neural Magic pedigree; its
# own README states FP8 KV cache support. Second choice if this fails:
# dbirks/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound (same 19.47GB, same packaging).
#
# This profile (qwen38-27b) is the REAL deployment target -- the FP8
# architecture smoke test itself runs from the separate, throwaway
# config/models/qwen38-27b-smoketest.env (tiny context, not for real
# traffic). This profile starts on the INT4 candidate directly since that
# is what can actually fit the 131072-context/0.968-utilization target on
# a single 32GB card -- see the decision tree above for why FP8 isn't
# viable here despite being upstream's own tuning target.
MODEL_ID=RedHatAI/Qwen3.8-27B-INT4
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=scar-coder

# Task's initial target -- matches the already-proven llama.cpp production
# config on this host. Fallback ladder if this doesn't fit the chosen
# quant's VRAM budget: 98304, then 65536, then 32768.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=131072

# Full-spec target per explicit user direction (plan §7.3, §25) -- deployed
# on the FIRST attempt, not swept up to from a conservative starting point.
# Still measured against real rocm-smi/amd-smi VRAM usage immediately after
# first load (not just vLLM's own log line) and backed off in small steps
# if real headroom is unsafe -- see docs/TUNING.md once that measurement is
# recorded.
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.968

# Leave empty unless the bake-off shows the checkpoint needs it forced
# (vLLM should read quant_method from the checkpoint's own config.json).
QUANTIZATION=

# Full-spec target per explicit user direction (plan §7.2, §25). This is a
# correctness gate, not just a throughput setting -- validate-model.sh must
# pass its known-answer/tool-call-determinism checks against this exact
# setting before it ships. If it fails, fall back to empty (model default).
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8

# Resolved via research 2026-09-14 (plan §24 open question 2, now
# answered): fetched Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B's own tokenizer_config.json
# chat_template directly -- it instructs XML-style tool calls
# (<tool_call><function=name><parameter=x>value</parameter></function></tool_call>),
# NOT Hermes-style bare JSON. qwen3_xml is the correct parser, not hermes.
# Still verify with scripts/test-tool-calling.sh before trusting it fully
# (vLLM's parser implementation could still have gaps against this exact
# template).
TOOL_CALL_PARSER=qwen3_xml

# Verified current parser name for the whole Qwen3 family (plan §5.1/§15).
REASONING_PARSER=qwen3

# Resolved 2026-09-14: R4D is controlled via RADIANCE_USE_R4D /
# RADIANCE_USE_R4D_GDN env vars (set in .env, default 1/on -- not a
# per-profile CLI flag), not something this field needs to carry. If R4D
# hard-refuses at startup for this checkpoint's weight format (plan §8.1's
# confirmed behavior -- verified as a hard refusal, not silent fallback),
# set RADIANCE_USE_R4D=0 and RADIANCE_USE_R4D_GDN=0 in .env and redeploy,
# rather than editing this field.
#
# DFlash2 activation flag is NOT YET CONFIRMED -- upstream docs describe
# tuning knobs (RADIANCE_DYNAMIC_DRAFT, RADIANCE_DRAFT_SCHEDULE,
# RADIANCE_DRAFT_TAU) but Phase 0 must run `vllm serve --help` inside the
# actual pulled image to find the enable/disable flag or speculative-config
# syntax this image expects -- do not guess it. Leave this field empty
# until confirmed; fill in once found. If DFlash2 fails its strict
# output-equivalence gate (plan §8.2), leave this empty (or try
# `--speculative-config '{"method":"ngram",...}'` if a quick ngram trial
# shows a real win).
SPEC_DECODE_ARGS=

# --language-model-only: required (plan §6, updated 2026-09-14) -- this
# model is a vision-language model (has a vision_config/ViT tower); this
# deployment only needs text/coding, so avoid loading/profiling the vision
# tower and free that VRAM for weights/KV-cache/activations instead. Same
# flag already proven on this host for the sibling Qwen3.6-27B deployment.
#
# --max-num-seqs 32: REQUIRED (found live 2026-09-14, first real deploy
# attempt). vLLM's default max_num_seqs=256 (built for multi-user
# throughput) failed hard at startup on this hybrid architecture:
# "ValueError: max_num_seqs (256) exceeds available Mamba cache blocks
# (194). Each decode sequence requires one Mamba cache block, so CUDA
# graph capture cannot proceed." This is a real, fixable constraint of
# the Gated-DeltaNet (Mamba-style) layers, not an architecture-compat
# failure -- each concurrent decode sequence needs its own Mamba state
# block, and the KV-budget-derived block count (194) is below the
# default concurrency ceiling. Since this deployment's stated priority is
# single-user interactive coding, not multi-user throughput (task spec),
# 32 is far more than needed and leaves comfortable margin under the 194
# limit -- raise only if real usage shows a need for more concurrent
# sequences, and never above 194 without also re-tuning
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION to grow the Mamba block budget.
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS=--trust-remote-code --language-model-only --max-num-seqs 32
